    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nInterested in this property? Sign up for mySherryFitz to arrange your viewing, see current offers or make your own offer. Register now at SherryFitz.ie.\n\nCoolishall is an impressive four-bedroom detached residence with a detached garage, ideally situated less than 3 km from Gorey town centre. Set behind a long tarmac driveway, the property offers generous off-street parking and is surrounded by beautifully landscaped grounds.The generous gardens provide an attractive setting for the home and offer excellent outdoor space for relaxing and entertaining.\n\nOn entering the main residence, it is immediately apparent that this is a substantial and beautifully maintained family home. Extending to approximately 180 sq. m., the property is bright, spacious and exceptionally well presented throughout. The current owners have tastefully decorated the interiors, creating a warm and welcoming home with a high standard of finish.\n\nThe well-proportioned accommodation briefly comprises an inviting living room with feature inset stove and fireplace, a separate sitting room with feature open fireplace, and a generous kitchen/dining room with bespoke fitted kitchen. A bright south-west facing sunroom enjoys an abundance of natural light and provides a wonderful connection to the gardens. The ground floor is completed by a utility room and bathroom.\n\nUpstairs, a bright and airy landing leads to four generously proportioned double bedrooms, including a principal bedroom with ensuite bathroom, together with a spacious family bathroom.\n\nCoolishall enjoys a highly convenient location, combining the tranquillity of a private residential setting with easy access to Gorey town and its extensive range of amenities. Gorey offers an excellent selection of shopping, dining and leisure facilities, including Gorey Shopping Centre, specialist retailers, restaurants, cafés, coffee shops and delis. The area is also well served by a wide range of sporting and recreational amenities, including local tennis, rugby, GAA and golf clubs, while Gorey Library provides an additional community resource.\nFor those who enjoy the coast and outdoor pursuits, the nearby seaside village of Courtown offers a range of marine and beachside activities. The property is also conveniently located for a selection of primary and secondary schools, making Coolishall an appealing choice for families seeking a spacious home in a well-connected yet peaceful setting.\n\nCoolishall combines generous accommodation, attractive private grounds and a convenient location to create an exceptional family home within easy reach of Gorey town."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nGROUND FLOOR - \n\n\nEntrance Hall - 1.7m x 6.3m\ntiled flooring.\n\nLiving Room - 8.0m x 6.0m\nwood flooring and feature inset stove fireplace.\n\nSitting Room - 7.4m x 5.5m\nwood flooring and feature open fireplace.\n\nKitchen/Dining Room - 5.8m x 3.3m\ntiled flooring and backsplash, bespoke fitted kitchen.\n\nSunroom - 3.5m x 4.0m\nat widest point, tiled flooring.\n\nUtility Room - 2.7m x 3.8m\nat widest point, tiled flooring and fitted storage units.\n\nBathroom - 1.3m x 3.8m\nat widest point, tiled flooring, w.c., wash hand basin and shower.\n\nFirst Floor - \n\n\nLanding - 2.9m x 5.1m\nat widest point, wood flooring.\n\nMaster Bedroom - 3.5m x 5.4m\nat widest point, wood flooring and built-in wardrobes.\n\nEnsuite - 2.2m x 1.7m\ntiled flooring, partially tiled walls, shower, w.c. and wash hand basin.\n\nBedroom 2 - 3.3m x 3.5m\nat widest point, wood flooring and built-in wardrobe.\n\nBedroom 3 - 4.0m x 3.4m\nwood flooring.\n\nBedroom 4 - 3.5m x 2.1m\nwood flooring.\n\nBathroom - 2.6m x 2.4m\ntiled floor and walls, bath, w.c. and wash hand basin.\n\n"
      },
